{:5850} ' &,53: logoff, also see &,53,a
' &,53[,idle]: stores idle in curdsp ($12e4, 4836): 0 = idle timer off,
' anything else = on. Also clears the chat page flag (53256) and sound
' repeat counter (962), re-links d1$ to the ML's live date string, and
' blanks status line columns 30-32.
' curdsp is restored afterwards. A pending chat page is cleared.
	&"{f6}&{comma}53 Logoff{f6:2}"
	q=peek(4836):x=q:&"curdsp before{colon}   {pound}!x{f6:2}"
' d1$: give it a value of its own, then let &,53 point it back at the clock
	d1$="test":&"d1$ set to{colon}      {quotation}"+d1$+"{quotation}{f6}"
	&,53:x=peek(4836):&"After &{comma}53{colon}     d1${equal}{quotation}"+d1$+"{quotation} (expect date){f6}"
	&"                curdsp{equal}{pound}!x (expect 0){f6}"
	&,53,1:x=peek(4836):&"After &{comma}53{comma}1{colon}   curdsp{equal}{pound}!x (expect 1){f6}"
	&,53,255:x=peek(4836):&"After &{comma}53{comma}255{colon} curdsp{equal}{pound}!x (expect 255){f6}"
' idle timer: does I= count on the sysop screen while curdsp is not 0?
' (only shown when the screen is in its normal mode)
	&,53,1:lp=1:&"{f6}Idle timer on{colon} watch for I{equal} counting on the sysop screen{comma} then hit a key{colon} {pound}g1{f6}"
	&,53,q:x=peek(4836):&"Restored{colon}       curdsp{equal}{pound}!x{f6}":return

